body:
BSc CSIT student here. My linked list program compiles fine but crashes with 'segmentation fault (core dumped)' when I try to delete a node from the middle. I suspect pointer issues. Here's my delete function:

```c
void deleteNode(Node *head, int key) {
  Node *curr = head;
  while (curr != NULL && curr->data != key) curr = curr->next;
  free(curr); // ???
}
```

answers.body:
The crash comes from freeing a node without updating the previous node's next pointer — and dereferencing memory you no longer own.

You need to keep a pointer to the previous node:

```c
void deleteNode(Node **head, int key) {
  Node *curr = *head, *prev = NULL;
  while (curr && curr->data != key) { prev = curr; curr = curr->next; }
  if (!curr) return; // not found
  if (prev) prev->next = curr->next; else *head = curr->next;
  free(curr);
}
```

Note the **double pointer** so you can update head when deleting the first node.
